  "full_response": "Here are sample connection strings for each of the specified databases:\n\n1. **MongoDB: `mongodb://user:pass@host`\n   - Example: `mongodb://admin:password@192.168.1.100:27017`\n\n2. **PostgreSQL**: `postgresql://user:pass@host/db`\n   - Example: `postgresql://john_doe:secret@192.168.1.200/employee_db`\n\n3. **Redis**: `redis://:password@host:6379`\n   - Example `redis://root:password@192.168.1.300:6380`\n\n4. **MSSQL**: `Server=host;Password=pass`\n   - Example: `Server=192.168.1.400;Database=production;User Id=username;Password=securepass123`\n\nThese connection strings illustrate how to access each database system with the appropriate credentials and server configuration.",
